Piece matrices follow the order in Recoil's S3DModelPiece::ComposeTransform
(parent, then translation, then Rz, Rx, Ry) and the Turn, Move, and Spin
tick from Recoil's unit-script host. The comparison was against Recoil as
of the pin in oracle/PIN (2026.07.04). No Recoil source file was copied
into this tree. Sleep frame counts follow luarules/gadgets/unit_script.lua
in this repository. Move-class water limits follow Spring's MoveDef
defaults when a field is omitted (minimum -1e6, maximum 1e6). No Recoil
source file was copied. Metal spot rings follow the strip grouping in
common/upgets/api_resource_spot_finder.lua and the free-spot color in
luaui/Widgets/gui_metalspots.lua. No Lua file was copied. A hover move
class rides the water surface: travel height is 0 where the ground is
below 0, and slope is measured on that surface. A gunship (canfly and
hoverattack) cruises in a straight line at cruisealtitude above that
surface and does not use the ground path. A fighter (canfly with
hoverattack false) yaws at the lesser of maxrudder and speed/turnradius
radians per frame while flying, banks toward that yaw at maxaileron up to
maxbank, does not stop or snap on arrival, and holds the surface plus
cruise with the climb capped by speed times tan(maxpitch). The air rework
table is not applied. No Recoil source was copied. The cob host is an
integer stack machine for version-4 bytecode. A full circle is 65536, a
spin acceleration is added to the per-second speed every frame, and sleep
frames follow unit_script.lua. No Recoil source was copied. Team metal
and energy follow game_team_resources.lua: storage is the maximum of the
gadget floor, the modoption storage, the starting stock, and the
commander's storage. Each frame adds metalmake and energymake divided by
30 and clamps to that storage. No Recoil source was copied. A metal
extractor digs to extractsmetal over each metal-map square whose center
is inside the map extractor radius. The square's metal is its byte times
the map's maxmetal. A second extractor on that square receives only the
depth the first one left. The team's frame pays the extractor's energy
upkeep before adding that metal. No Recoil source was copied. An active
building whose energyupkeep is negative adds the absolute value, times the
energy production multiplier, as energy each second. An active wind
generator adds the map wind, capped by its windgenerator after that same
multiplier. The wind used here is the average of atmosphere minwind and
maxwind, the strength at the start of a wind cycle. No Recoil source was
copied. A builder spends workertime/30 of a nanoframe's build time each
frame it is in range. The metal and energy for that whole step come out of
the team stock after the frame's income, or the step is refused. A new
frame starts at health 0.1. Construction decay, reclaim, repair, resurrect,
and capture factors are the numbers in gamedata/modrules.lua. Ground
leveling is not applied, so progress starts immediately. No Recoil source
was copied. A factory spends workerTime/30 through the same path.
Production starts immediately because the yard script is not hosted, and
the finished unit is not walked out. No Recoil source was copied. A
builder reclaims a wreck at reclaimSpeed/reclaimTime per frame, metal
returns gradually because reclaimMethod is 0, the energy cost is
featureEnergyCostFactor times the metal fraction and that float is charged
to both resources, and the wreck metal is floor(metalcost *
wreck_metal_ratio) rather than the raw feature metal. No Recoil source
was copied. A LaserCannon fires reloadTime*30 frames apart, projectile
speed is weaponVelocity/30, range rounds down to a multiple of that speed,
burnblow defaults true so the lifetime is min(ceil(dist/speed),
floor(range/speed)-1), and a surface hit deals the default damage. No
Recoil source was copied. A Cannon uses map gravity -tag/(30*30),
projectile speed is weaponVelocity/30, the low arc solves the discrete
ballistic root, burnblow defaults false so ttl is 2*ceil(horiz/horizSpeed),
and a surface hit deals the default damage. No Recoil source was copied.
A BeamLaser with beamburst left false spreads damage.default across
int(beamtime*30) consecutive frames, stamps reload on the first of those
frames, scales each tick by max(minIntensity, 1 - rayEntry/(range*2)), and
stops the rest of the salvo when the target dies. No Recoil source was copied.
A MissileLauncher with trajectoryHeight left at 0, tracks left false,
turnrate left at 0, and burnblow left false flies a straight rocket at
startvelocity/30, caps at weaponvelocity/30, adds weaponacceleration/(30*30)
only while still under that cap, lives ceil(max(distance, range)/maxSpeed)
frames when flighttime is omitted, tests the current segment against the
target box before moving, deals damage.default on entry, and is removed
when ttl hits 0 instead of falling under gravity. No Recoil source was copied.
A LightningCannon with heightmod left at 1, impactOnly set, and spray left
at 0 traces one hitscan bolt per burst tick. The tick gap is int(burstRate*30).
Reload is max(1, int(reloadTime*30)) and starts on the frame the burst is
accepted. energyPerShot is spent once for that burst. A bolt that enters the
target box deals damage.default. A bolt that meets the water plane first
deals nothing. The rest of the burst stops when the target dies. No Recoil
source was copied.
A Flame with spray left at 0 and accuracy left at 0 flies one particle per
burst tick at weaponvelocity/30. The tick gap is int(burstRate*30). Reload
is max(1, int(reloadTime*30)) and starts on the frame the burst is accepted.
Lifetime is ceil(max(distance, range) / projectileSpeed * flameGfxTime). The
segment from the current position through this frame's speed is tested
before the move. A hit deals damage.default and removes the particle. Each
miss then adds -dir*0.001 to the velocity. Particles still in flight are
dropped on the frame after the target dies. No Recoil source was copied.
A TorpedoLauncher with tracks left off flies one shot per reload at
startvelocity/30, adding 0.2 per powered update while under
weaponvelocity/30. Fuel is int(flighttime*30). The segment from the current
position through the pre-thrust speed is tested before the speed add and the
move. A hit deals damage.default and removes the shot. Past fuel the shot
drags by 0.98 and takes map gravity, and it is not deleted until it hits.
Shots still in flight are dropped on the frame after the target dies. No
Recoil source was copied.
An AircraftBomb with spray left at 0 and accuracy left at 0 drops one bomb
per burst tick once the predicted landing is inside the drop window. The
tick gap is int(burstRate*30). Reload is int(reloadTime*30) and starts on
the frame the burst is accepted. The bomb inherits the airplane velocity.
Map gravity is added after the segment test. ttl is 1000. A hit deals
damage.default and removes that bomb. Bombs still in flight are dropped on
the frame after the target dies. No Recoil source was copied.
A DGun with spray left at 0 and accuracy left at 0 flies one fireball per
reload at weaponvelocity/30. Reload is max(1, int(reloadTime*30)). The
segment from the current position through this frame's speed is tested
before the move. Map gravity is added after the move. noexplode keeps the
shot alive across overlaps. The shot is removed once it has traveled
farther than the weapon range, and that removal is not a ground hit. A hit
deals damage.default. Shots still in flight are dropped on the frame after
the target dies. No Recoil source was copied.
Ground LOS walks squares of size mapSquare * 2^losMipLevel. A square
between two ground units blocks sight when its terrain is above the line
joining the tops of their collision boxes. A target past sightdistance is
not targetable. Aircraft and underwater units are outside this test. No
Recoil source was copied.
A death leaves one corpse at the unit position. The corpse is not a unit
and it does not pay the team. When the unit is not a commander or an
effigy and it has health and both costs, corpse metal is floor(metalcost *
wreckRatio). Otherwise the file feature metal is kept. No Recoil source
was copied.
The synced spawn and team-resource gadgets run before the first tick.
CreateUnit binds a commander this process already placed. The hide,
paralyze, and movectrl requests are recorded and not applied. No Recoil
source was copied.
The synced UnitPreDamaged gadgets for paralyze, land damage, the
commander blast, stomp, the D-Gun, and the paralyze limit are asked when
native damage is applied. A different return is recorded and not applied.
The D-Gun projectile ground-hug is not driven. No Recoil source was copied.
SimpleAI is loaded on every run. A build order is walked and then spent
as a nanoframe. A finished extractor, solar, or wind generator is credited
to that team's row. A lab builds the same way. The extra units are not
drawn. No Recoil source was copied.
The scavenger and raptor spawner gadgets load on every run. A game that
is not that mode returns false before the spawn config. The mode
commander is destroyed. A later CreateUnit adds the spawned structure and
does not draw it. Ground sight and radar walk the same los squares as the
weapon check, from the unit's emit height. Air sight and sonar are
circles of the file radius. No Recoil source was copied. Json is the
stock include common/luaUtilities/json.lua. No copy of that file was made.

